/-!
# The graded ideal generated by a submodule in one degree, its quotient situation, and the
morphism of relative Projs

In Situation 0849 let `𝒜` be the quasi-coherent graded `𝒪_X`-algebra on the algebraic space `X`
over `S`, and let `ℐ ⊆ 𝒜` be a graded ideal — in every degree a submodule of the homogeneous
piece, stable under multiplication by a homogeneous local section, with no quasi-coherence
assumed.  The main example is the graded ideal `ℱ𝒜` generated by a submodule `ℱ ⊆ 𝒜_d`, which is
the ideal the statements of Stacks 085M and 085N are about.  This file constructs `ℱ𝒜`, the
quotient `𝒜/ℐ` as the algebra of a new Situation 0849 on the same space, the quotient
homomorphism `𝒜 ⟶ 𝒜/ℐ`, and the induced morphism `Proj_X(𝒜/ℐ) ⟶ Proj_X(𝒜)` of the relative
Projs of Stacks 084A–084C, and proves that it is a closed immersion whose base change to every
scheme point `f : T ⟶ X` is the morphism of Stacks 07ZG for `f^*𝒜 ⟶ f^*(𝒜/ℐ)`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.MulStableGradedSubmodule`: a graded ideal of the
  algebra of a situation: a submodule of each homogeneous piece, stable under multiplication.
  Quasi-coherence of the pieces is not part of the data; it is carried as the hypothesis `hℐ`
  where it is needed.  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.GradedIdeal` of
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.RelativeProjQuotientSituation` is the notion that bundles
  quasi-coherence.)
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.generatedByDegree` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.degreeIdeal`: the graded ideal `ℱ𝒜` generated by
  a submodule `ℱ ⊆ 𝒜_d`, degree by degree (`SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.generatedInDegree`) and
  as a graded ideal.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.MulStableGradedSubmodule.toIdeal`: a graded
  ideal of the situation as a two-sided graded ideal `SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.Ideal` of `𝒜`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.quotientAlgebra`: the quotient `𝒜/ℐ`, which is
  `SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.Ideal.quotient`, the degreewise sheafification of the sectionwise
  quotient.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.quotient`: **Situation 0849 for `𝒜/ℐ`**.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.quotientHom`: the quotient homomorphism.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.quotientHomPoints`: the quotient homomorphism read
  over the scheme points of the base, between the presentations of Stacks 084B.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.quotientProjHom`: **the morphism
  `Proj_X(𝒜/ℐ) ⟶ Proj_X(𝒜)`** of Stacks 085F, defined everywhere by Stacks 085H (1).

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.mul_mem_generatedByDegree`: `ℱ𝒜` is an ideal, and
  `…generatedByDegree_add_eq_closedSubspaceDegreeProducts`: in degree `d + e` it is the ideal
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.closedSubspaceDegreeProducts` of Stacks 085M.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.quotientMkIsColimit`: `(𝒜/ℐ)_n` is the cokernel
  of `ℐ_n ⟶ 𝒜_n`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.isClosedImmersion_quotientProjHom`: the morphism
  `Proj_X(𝒜/ℐ) ⟶ Proj_X(𝒜)` is a closed immersion of algebraic spaces.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.isPullback_quotientFibreMap`: its base change
  to a scheme point `f : T ⟶ X` is the morphism `Proj_T(f^*(𝒜/ℐ)) ⟶ Proj_T(f^*𝒜)` of Stacks
  07ZG, through the identifications of Stacks 084B (2).
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.range_eq_range_quotientProjHom_of_fibre`: a
  subsheaf of `Proj_X(𝒜)` whose pullback to the fibre over one surjective étale scheme point is
  `Proj_W(w^*(𝒜/ℐ))` is `Proj_X(𝒜/ℐ)`.

## What is not proved

The pieces of `ℱ𝒜` are not shown to be quasi-coherent here (the source reads `ℱ𝒜_n` as the image
of `ℱ ⊗ 𝒜_{n-d} ⟶ 𝒜_n`); the quotient situation takes quasi-coherence of the ideal as the
hypothesis `hℐ`, which is part of the notion of a quasi-coherent graded ideal, not a result of the
source being assumed.

## Implementation notes

The quotient `𝒜/ℐ` is the quotient `SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.Ideal.quotient` of a sheaf of
graded algebras by a two-sided graded ideal (the ideal absorbs multiplication on both sides because
`𝒜` is commutative): the sectionwise quotient is a graded algebra of presheaves of modules, and
`Stacks.GradedAlgebra.sheafify` sheafifies it degreewise.
The sheafification is available because the module universe is the universe `u` of the schemes,
at which the small étale site is essentially small; this is why the file works in
`RelativeProjSituation.{u, u}`, the universe of Stacks 085M and 085N in this tree.

The size field of Situation 0849 for `𝒜/ℐ` is not formal: sections of a sheafified quotient over a
non-affine chart are not quotients of the sections of `𝒜`.  It is supplied by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.hasCardinalLT_sections_of_epi` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.RelativeProjQuotientSituation`, applied to the degreewise
quotient homomorphism, which is an epimorphism.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0849](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0849)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 084B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/084B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 085F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/085F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 085H](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/085H)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 085N](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/085N)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07ZG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07ZG)
-/

